sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-anolis-carolinensis-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anolis-carolinensis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anolis-carolinensis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Anolis carolinensis Schnakenberg wavelength at 101.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 85.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2. The same Schnakenberg field (a = 0.055, b = 0.945, D_v/D_u = 8.2, λ_c = 101.1 µm, Holocene 0 Ma). Nonlinear periodic peak 99.82 µm; Neumann peak 103.96 µm; dispersion Pearson r = 0.9941. Across 72–168 µm the measured peaks are a factor 0.971 of the onset prediction (Pearson r = 1.0 because the bias is proportional; RMSE = 3.45 µm; KS = 0.167, p ≈ 1 at n = 6). Ablation with D_v = D_u drops the amplitude by a factor 1220. The 512 px, 12-frame GIF scores 88.9 against the Commons specimen on the fitness-test orientation, radial-FFT and coherency similarity. Specimen structure-tensor coherency is 0.6275 against 0.5308 on the rendered field. Weighted overall 85.4. Image fitness 0.55*88.9 + 0.30*76 + 0.15*90 = 85.2. Overall 85.4/100 (faithfulness 84.1, reproducibility 88.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/anolis_carolinensis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-anolis-carolinensis-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 466662 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 a5272637322b843ecaee43a0898221e93786df5eb5d952714b4a99cc6f3db99b (sha256 a5272637322b843ecaee43a0898221e93786df5eb5d952714b4a99cc6f3db99b), spec_fingerprint 17ba2b079a1597562250107c46da2253ac6d3c2a7a7816f161aca05a741fc46e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 17ba2b079a1597562250107c46da2253ac6d3c2a7a7816f161aca05a741fc46e; artifact_sha256: a5272637322b843ecaee43a0898221e93786df5eb5d952714b4a99cc6f3db99b. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-anolis-carolinensis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v. | Alexander & Fahrenbach 1969: xanthophore, iridophore and basal melanophore layers in A. carolinensis; melanin in the processes turns the skin from green toward brown. | Taylor & Hadley 1970: physiological melanosome migration, not a new wavelength, is the colour-change mechanism inside one melanophore.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u and D_v are chosen so k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v) equals (2π/101.1 µm)^2. | Eight wavelengths on an 808.8 µm patch; a 40 µm cellular predecessor holds zero critical modes. | The nonlinear FFT peak sits at 0.971 of the onset wavelength on every swept target. That factor is the reported residual.; transfer_boundary: Fofonjka & Milinkovitch 2021 (Timon scale borders quantising RD into a cellular automaton) is the organ-scale successor, not this intra-scale 101.1 µm patch.; does_not_claim: That Alexander & Fahrenbach measured 101.1 µm as a Turing wavelength. | That the rendered spot field is a photograph of the animal. CV similarity 88.9 is a texture score, not an identity claim. | A fossil chronospecies. The series is Holocene only (1/1, 0 Ma).." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=1.3]: A second assessor from another provider has not scored this slot.",
            "open need [provenance_lock/repro-package, pressure P=0.9]: Nanopub profile is absent, so the trig files cannot be signed or trusty-checked.",
            "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=2.8]: Need a dermal micrograph at ~100 µm, not only the whole-animal Commons portrait.",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml. Nanopubs were built and conformance-checked, not signed.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Single builder-assessor. No independent second score.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'One whole-animal photograph. A 101 µm dermal micrograph is still absent, so specimen-match stays a texture score.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.854"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

